<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><strong>Effective Date: January 15, 2026</strong></p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>DOGFOOD 2026 ("we", "us", "our") operates the DOGFOOD 2026 hackathon platform. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, and protect information about you when you use the Platform.</p>

<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>We collect the following categories of information:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Name and email address provided during registration.</li>
  <li><strong>Submission Data:</strong> Project titles, summaries, repository URLs, and submission timestamps.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Session identifiers stored in cookies, and action logs (audit trail) recording platform activity such as score submissions and project edits.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use collected information to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Operate and maintain the Platform and the hackathon event.</li>
  <li>Assign projects to judges and facilitate scoring.</li>
  <li>Communicate with participants about event updates.</li>
  <li>Detect and prevent abuse, fraud, or violations of our Terms of Service.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Cookies</h2>
<p>The Platform uses a single session cookie to authenticate users. This cookie contains a random session identifier. No tracking cookies or third-party analytics scripts are used.</p>

<h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. Project submissions are visible to other Platform users as part of the public project gallery. Judge scores are visible only to organizers and the submitting judge. We may disclose information if required by law.</p>

<h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
<p>Event data, including submissions and scores, is retained for 12 months following the conclusion of the hackathon. Account data is deleted upon written request.</p>

<h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
<p>You have the right to access, correct, or request deletion of your personal data. To exercise these rights, contact us at <strong>organizer@example.org</strong>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

<h2>8. Security</h2>
<p>We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your data. Session identifiers are stored as HTTP-only cookies. The SQLite database is stored on a volume accessible only to the application container.</p>

<h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The Platform is not directed at children under 16. If you believe we have inadvertently collected data from a minor, contact us immediately for deletion.</p>

<h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically. The effective date at the top of this page will reflect the most recent version.</p>

<h2>11. Contact</h2>
<p>Privacy inquiries: <strong>organizer@example.org</strong></p>

